# Validation Checklist (SOLID-Compliant)

## Immediate Validation (Priority Order)

### 1. Parent Structure Validation (DO THIS FIRST!)

**⚠️ CRITICAL: After removing large JSX blocks, validate parent structure IMMEDIATELY**

```bash
# Count tags
grep -c "<div" parent.tsx
grep -c "</div>" parent.tsx
# Should be equal

# PowerShell validation
$content = Get-Content "parent.tsx" -Raw
$openDivs = ([regex]::Matches($content, '<div')).Count
$closeDivs = ([regex]::Matches($content, '</div>')).Count
Write-Host "Open: $openDivs, Close: $closeDivs, Diff: $($openDivs - $closeDivs)"
# Should be 0 difference
```

**Why this matters:**
- Removing 3,400+ lines can break parent structure
- Parent structure issues cause cascading errors
- Fix parent FIRST, then move to child component

### 2. JSX Structure Validation (Child Component)

**Verify balanced tags:**

```bash
# Count opening and closing divs
grep -c "<div" component.tsx
grep -c "</div>" component.tsx
# Should be equal

# Check for:
# - Matching opening/closing tags
# - Proper nesting
# - No orphaned tags
# - Unclosed conditionals
```

### 3. SRP Validation (Single Responsibility Principle)

**Check component responsibilities:**

- [ ] Component has single, clear responsibility
- [ ] Business logic extracted to hooks/services
- [ ] UI rendering separated from logic
- [ ] Component under size limits:
  - Presentational: Max 200 lines
  - Container: Max 300 lines
  - Hook: Max 150 lines
  - Service: Max 100 lines
- [ ] No "God Component" anti-pattern
- [ ] Functions count within limits:
  - Component: Max 5 functions
  - Hook: Max 8 functions
  - Service: Max 10 methods

### 4. DIP Validation (Dependency Inversion Principle)

**Check dependency injection:**

- [ ] Dependencies injected, not imported directly
- [ ] Services use interfaces, not concrete classes
- [ ] Easy to mock for testing
- [ ] No direct imports of services in components
- [ ] Service interfaces defined
- [ ] Components depend on abstractions

**Example check:**
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Direct import (violates DIP)
import { uploadDocument } from '@/app/onboarding/actions'

// ✅ GOOD: Injected service (follows DIP)
interface ComponentProps {
  documentService: DocumentService // Interface
}
```

### 5. ISP Validation (Interface Segregation Principle)

**Check interface segregation:**

- [ ] Component props < 10
- [ ] Props are focused and necessary
- [ ] No unused props passed down
- [ ] Large interfaces split into smaller ones
- [ ] Components don't depend on props they don't use

**Example check:**
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Too many props (violates ISP)
interface Props {
  // 20+ props
}

// ✅ GOOD: Segregated interfaces (follows ISP)
interface ContainerProps { /* 5 props */ }
interface ListProps { /* 3 props */ }
interface FormProps { /* 4 props */ }
```

### 6. OCP Validation (Open/Closed Principle)

**Check extensibility:**

- [ ] Component extensible via props/children
- [ ] No hardcoded behavior
- [ ] Uses composition over modification
- [ ] Can extend without modifying existing code

### 7. TypeScript Validation

**⚠️ Do comprehensive type audit, not iterative fixes:**

```bash
# Find ALL potential implicit any issues:
grep -n "\.map(" component.tsx | grep -v ":"
grep -n "\.filter(" component.tsx | grep -v ":"
grep -n "\.some(" component.tsx | grep -v ":"
grep -n "prev =>" component.tsx

# Fix ALL at once:
# 1. Add type annotations to all callback parameters
# 2. Add type annotations to all map/filter/some callbacks
# 3. Fix all state type definitions
# 4. Verify all props types
```

**Run TypeScript compiler:**
```bash
npm run build
# OR
npx tsc --noEmit
```

### 8. Runtime Validation

**Test the component:**
- [ ] Navigate to the page
- [ ] Verify component renders
- [ ] Test all interactions
- [ ] Check console for errors
- [ ] Verify lazy loading works
- [ ] Test all modals/forms
- [ ] Test all filters/search

## Post-Extraction Checklist

### Code Quality (SOLID Compliance)
- [ ] All TypeScript errors resolved
- [ ] All props properly typed
- [ ] All imports are correct
- [ ] No unused imports
- [ ] No unused variables
- [ ] Code is properly formatted
- [ ] SRP compliance verified
- [ ] DIP compliance verified
- [ ] ISP compliance verified
- [ ] OCP compliance verified

### Functionality
- [ ] Component renders correctly
- [ ] All interactions work
- [ ] All modals/forms work
- [ ] All filters/search work
- [ ] All data displays correctly
- [ ] No console errors

### Performance
- [ ] Component lazy loads correctly
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders
- [ ] Bundle size is acceptable
- [ ] Performance is improved (if that was the goal)

### Maintainability
- [ ] Component is self-contained
- [ ] Props interface is clear
- [ ] Code is well-organized
- [ ] Comments are added where needed
- [ ] Component is testable
- [ ] Services are mockable (DIP)

## Validation Priority Order

**ALWAYS validate in this order:**

1. **Parent Structure** ← DO THIS FIRST (after removing large blocks)
2. **JSX Structure** ← DO SECOND (balanced tags)
3. **SRP Compliance** ← Check responsibilities
4. **DIP Compliance** ← Check dependency injection
5. **ISP Compliance** ← Check prop count and focus
6. **TypeScript Types** ← Comprehensive audit
7. **Runtime Functionality** ← Test in browser

**Why this order matters:**
- Structure issues cascade to other errors
- SOLID violations cause maintainability issues
- Type errors are easier to fix after structure is correct
- Runtime testing is last because it requires everything else to work
